            "review_title": "Review at Cháo Xưa 29",
            "review_text": "An T\n1 contribution\n0\n“A Taste of Home at Cháo Xưa”\nNov 2025 • Solo\nVery delicious especially Bánh Đa Cháo Xưa is a small, cozy place that truly captures the taste of the countryside. Their bánh đa kê is soft and fragrant, with nutty millet and crispy rice paper that makes each bite unforgettable. The black bean porridge is simple yet delicious — mildly sweet, with tender beans cooked just right, perfect for breakfast or a late afternoon meal. The owner is kind and friendly, service is quick, and prices are very reasonable. If you love traditional Vietnamese flavors, this spot will bring you right back to the comforting taste of home.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten November 2, 2025",
